---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const releases = [
  { v: '5.0.6', d: 'August 2026', items: ['Financial dashboard with rule-based deal health scorecard and action centre', 'Partner Commentary: enriched commentary using management explanations', 'Group Consolidation across entity trial balances', 'Export to PowerPoint: table, commentary or both, multi-sheet', 'Data Masking configuration before AI calls', 'Update TB: add a later period without rebuilding'] },
  { v: '5.0.0', d: 'July 2026', items: ['Managed AI backend replaces bring-your-own-key', 'Run Full FDD: P&L, BS, NWC, net debt and cash flow from a mapped TB', 'Trial balance translation and AI mapping', 'Doc Triage and Deal Documents for CIMs and transcripts', 'Management Questions with MQ log', 'Sector Data Book and Deal Brief'] },
  { v: '4.2.0', d: 'April 2026', items: ['EBITDA Bridge with waterfall chart and P&L cross-check', 'Databook Builder', 'Export to Word', 'Remote prompt library', 'Code-signed installer and auto-update flow'] },
];
---
<Base title="ZAF Tools Changelog: Release Notes for the Excel Add-in" description="Release history for the ZAF Tools Excel add-in: new FDD features, AI modules, template library additions and fixes in each version." crumbs={[{name:'Changelog',href:'/changelog'}]}>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:1.5rem"><div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Changelog</h1>
    <p>ZAF Tools ships updates every 4–8 weeks. This page lists what changed in each release: new FDD workflows, AI modules, template library additions, and fixes. If you're deciding whether ZAF Tools is actively developed, or whether a feature you need has shipped yet, this is the page to check.</p>
    <p>Two kinds of releases show up here. Feature releases add a new workflow or module — the move from manual EBITDA bridge building to <code>Run Full FDD</code> across five statements is the kind of change that shows up as a major version bump (5.0.0, July 2026). Maintenance releases add smaller things inside an existing workflow — a new export format, a template library addition, a fix to a mapping edge case — and land as minor versions.</p>
    <p>Every release is installed automatically for existing users through the code-signed auto-update flow; there's nothing to download by hand. If you're on an older version and a workflow described on a feature page doesn't match what you see in Excel, check the version number against this page — it's usually a sign an update is pending or blocked by IT policy.</p>
    <p>The releases below are grouped from newest to oldest. Each line is a shipped, user-facing change — not every internal fix is listed.</p>
    {releases.map(r => <><div class="bar"><h2>Version {r.v}</h2><span>{r.d}</span></div><ul>{r.items.map(i => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul></>)}
    <h3>What's next</h3>
    <p>The roadmap is driven by what deal teams ask for during live demos, not a fixed release calendar. Recent releases — Group Consolidation, the deal health scorecard, Partner Commentary — all started as a specific request from a boutique or PE deal team running a real engagement. If there's a workflow your team rebuilds by hand every deal and doesn't see here, <a href="/start-trial?type=demo">book a demo</a> and it becomes an input to the next release, not just a feature request in a queue.</p>
    <h3>How releases reach you</h3>
    <p>The ZAF Tools installer is code-signed and updates automatically — most users are on the latest version within a few days of release, subject to their firm's IT update policy. Enterprise deployments on a locked-down image can pin to a specific version; talk to us before upgrading a firm-wide install mid-engagement.</p>
    <p>See also: <a href="/features">what ZAF Tools does today</a>, or <a href="/pricing">how the pricing works</a> if a release above has moved something from Enterprise to a lower plan.</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
